### The Core Revelation: System Hierarchy

We defined the definitive hierarchy for task management:

1.  **Level 1: Session (Primary)** - Work happens here. [task.md](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/task.md) owned by session.
2.  **Level 2: Brain (Storage)** - Persisted items. User moves unclosed work here.
3.  **Level 3: PEFS (Safety Net)** - Auto-detects slips in Brain. Ages them. Reminds you.

**Rule:** Session is the center. Brain is storage. PEFS is the safety net.

### Strategic Conclusion: Agent-Tool Fit

We analyzed why the 50+ tool suite wasn't being used ([NUCLEUS_ECOSYSTEM_ANALYSIS.md](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/NUCLEUS_ECOSYSTEM_ANALYSIS.md)) and defined the fix:

**Don't dump 50 tools on one agent.**
- **Synthesizer:** Uses Files (Whiteboard)
